   "text": "The schedule below shows the marginal cost of a firm in a perfectly competitive market.\n\n| Output (units) | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 8 | 9 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Marginal cost ($) | 5 | 5.5 | 6 | 6.5 | 7 | 8 | 9.5 |\n\nSuppose the rental of the machine hired, a fixed cost, increases by \\$2 while the marginal cost for each unit of the output is reduced by \\$0.5. As a result, the profit-maximising output of the firm \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ while the profit of the firm \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n\n- A. increases ...... decreases\n- B. increases ...... may increase or decrease\n- C. decreases ...... decreases\n- D. decreases ...... may increase or decrease",
   "html": "<p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The schedule below shows the marginal cost of a firm in a perfectly competitive market.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Output (units)</th>\n<th>3</th>\n<th>4</th>\n<th>5</th>\n<th>6</th>\n<th>7</th>\n<th>8</th>\n<th>9</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Marginal cost ($)</td>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>5.5</td>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>6.5</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>9.5</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Suppose the rental of the machine hired, a fixed cost, increases by \\$2 while the marginal cost for each unit of the output is reduced by \\$0.5. As a result, the profit-maximising output of the firm __________ while the profit of the firm __________.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A. increases ...... decreases</li>\n<li>B. increases ...... may increase or decrease</li>\n<li>C. decreases ...... decreases</li>\n<li>D. decreases ...... may increase or decrease</li>\n</ul>",
