   "html": "<p>38.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Initially an economy operates at the long-run equilibrium. Which of the following will lead to a deflationary (output) gap in the economy?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A. The government increases the salaries tax rate.</li>\n<li>B. The government reduces the profits tax rate.</li>\n<li>C. The government invests in the construction of a cross-border express rail link.</li>\n<li>D. The central bank reduces the required reserve ratio.</li>\n</ul>",
