   "text": "Assume the labour input requirements for the production of computers and toys in Japan and Hong Kong are as follows:\n\n| | 1 unit of computers | 1 unit of toys |\n|---|---|---|\n| Japan | 2 man-hours | 6 man-hours |\n| Hong Kong | 4 man-hours | 8 man-hours |\n\nSuppose there is no transportation cost. Which of the following can be the terms of trade so that trade is mutually beneficial to Japan and Hong Kong?\n\n- A. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 0.4 units of toys\n- B. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 0.5 units of toys\n- C. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 1 unit of toys\n- D. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 2.5 units of toys",
   "html": "<p>40.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Assume the labour input requirements for the production of computers and toys in Japan and Hong Kong are as follows:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>1 unit of computers</th>\n<th>1 unit of toys</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Japan</td>\n<td>2 man-hours</td>\n<td>6 man-hours</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hong Kong</td>\n<td>4 man-hours</td>\n<td>8 man-hours</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Suppose there is no transportation cost. Which of the following can be the terms of trade so that trade is mutually beneficial to Japan and Hong Kong?</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 0.4 units of toys</li>\n<li>B. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 0.5 units of toys</li>\n<li>C. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 1 unit of toys</li>\n<li>D. 1 unit of computers exchanges for 2.5 units of toys</li>\n</ul>",
