   "html": "<p>12.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Let $\\mathrm{f}(x)=4x(x+1)^{2}+ax+b$ , where $a$ and $b$ are constants. It is given that $x-3$ is a factor of $\\mathrm{f}(x)$ . When $\\mathrm{f}(x)$ is divided by $x+2$ , the remainder is $2b+165$ .\n(a) Find $a$ and $b$ .\n(3 marks)\n(b) Someone claims that the equation $\\mathrm{f}(x)=0$ has at least one irrational root. Do you agree? Explain your answer.\n(4 marks)</p>",
